WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.460
- [Narrator] Located in
central London is a public park

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.125
that remains hidden to even the locals.

00:00:08.125 --> 00:00:10.958
(inspiring music)

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.280
The medieval style church
of St. Dunstan in the East

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.460
was built in around 1100

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.520
and has had a long 900-year-old history.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.240
In 1666, it was rebuilt
after being damaged

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.250
in the Great Fire of London.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.210
Then, during World War II,

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.340
a direct hit during the London Blitz

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.510
destroyed a majority of the structure,

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:37.163
leaving behind only the north
and south walls and steeple.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.520
Instead of rebuilding once again,

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.910
the city of London decided
to turn the remains

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.810
of St. Dunstan in the East
into the public garden,

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.900
which is accessible today
if you know where to look.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.910
Tucked away from the main
road, the garden is situated

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.020
between the Tower of
London and London Bridge.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.460
The green, ivy-covered
walls, trees and flowers

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.870
offer an enchanting escape from the city

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.503
and serve as a reminder
of London's history.

